cellacdc/shared/widgets/style.py.doc:
Widget style constants and the pyqtgraph colormap setup, run once at import.

shared/widgets/__init__.py imports this module, so importing any shared widget module runs it first. On import it:

- sets pyqtgraph's row-major image axis order;
- renames and removes pyqtgraph colormap presets (renamePgCmaps, removeHSVcmaps) and registers cividis, cool, sunset, tab20 and tab10 (addGradients), which gives cmaps, Gradients, GradientsLabels and GradientsImage (the gradient editor items of lut_items.py use these dict objects, never copies);
- computes the stylesheets and colors of the current color scheme (LINEEDIT_WARNING_STYLESHEET, LINEEDIT_INVALID_ENTRY_STYLESHEET, TREEWIDGET_STYLESHEET, LISTWIDGET_STYLESHEET, BASE_COLOR, PROGRESSBAR_QCOLOR, PROGRESSBAR_HIGHLIGHTEDTEXT_QCOLOR, TEXT_COLOR) and the default widget font.

Colormaps saved by users are read from custom_cmaps_filepath (getCustomGradients). Read it through this module at call time: the tests redirect it to a temporary folder. nonInvertibleCmaps lists the colormaps that baseHistogramLUTitem does not invert. Leaf module: it imports no other widget module.
